WEBVTT

00:43.043 --> 00:44.503
Really? He said that?

00:44.587 --> 00:45.796
CHAPTER 50:
A CLASSIC, NOT A CLICHÉ

00:45.880 --> 00:46.964
He really did.

00:49.091 --> 00:50.634
How's this one?

00:50.718 --> 00:51.552
No.

00:52.553 --> 00:53.387
Then this one?

00:56.807 --> 00:59.435
The problem is
we don't know what he likes.

00:59.518 --> 01:01.270
Does he like sweet or sexy?

01:02.980 --> 01:05.232
I think he probably likes sweet and sexy.

01:05.941 --> 01:07.485
He looks kind of greedy, right?

01:08.402 --> 01:09.528
Oh, wait a second.

01:10.029 --> 01:12.323
VIDEO CHATTING
EUI-JU, GO-YA

01:12.406 --> 01:13.574
Huh?

01:15.576 --> 01:16.410
Ta-da.

01:17.953 --> 01:19.121
Are you for real?

01:19.955 --> 01:20.790
Then again,

01:21.582 --> 01:23.834
this won't cut it, right?

01:23.918 --> 01:25.127
Not for our first date.

01:26.378 --> 01:27.213
Eui-ju.

01:28.130 --> 01:28.964
Yes, sir?

01:29.840 --> 01:30.841
Are you free this Saturday?

01:32.635 --> 01:35.054
What does he want to say to me

01:35.137 --> 01:37.973
that he suggested a private meeting
on the weekend?

01:40.392 --> 01:41.852
Oh, my.

01:43.896 --> 01:45.940
So what should I wear?

01:49.235 --> 01:52.071
Why is it still only Thursday?

01:56.492 --> 01:58.369
Why is it still only Friday?

02:00.871 --> 02:03.624
It's finally tomorrow.

02:03.707 --> 02:06.710
Why is time going so slowly?

02:21.350 --> 02:22.476
Welcome.

02:22.560 --> 02:23.394
EPISODE 16

02:23.477 --> 02:24.520
Do you have a reservation?

02:24.603 --> 02:26.063
Yes, I believe so.

02:26.146 --> 02:27.523
What name is it in?

02:27.606 --> 02:28.649
Ga Woo-su.

02:31.193 --> 02:32.653
I don't see one in that name.

02:34.697 --> 02:36.407
Then, Yeo Eui-ju?

02:38.701 --> 02:39.952
Not in that one either.

02:41.370 --> 02:42.538
Then, a table for two, please.

02:42.621 --> 02:44.540
-Yes, please follow me.
-Yes.

02:51.797 --> 02:53.799
-Can I get you some water?
-Sure.

02:57.136 --> 02:59.138
-Please let me know if you need anything.
-Okay.

03:05.227 --> 03:07.563
What do I do? I'm so freaking nervous.

03:08.147 --> 03:10.316
Don't show it too much.
It's not a good look.

03:11.692 --> 03:13.485
Don't forget to order cream pasta, okay?

03:14.111 --> 03:15.821
That's such a cliché.

03:17.197 --> 03:18.949
It's a classic, not a cliché.

03:19.033 --> 03:20.367
Just trust me and try it.

03:31.337 --> 03:32.713
Welcome.

03:54.902 --> 03:57.655
I guess he invited us so we can make up.

03:59.198 --> 04:00.157
I guess so.

04:07.289 --> 04:08.332
Welcome.

04:08.832 --> 04:09.750
You got here early.

04:09.833 --> 04:12.419
-Do you have a reservation?
-Yes, after-school for 12 people.

04:13.212 --> 04:14.922
I don't have one for after-school,

04:15.005 --> 04:16.548
but I have one for Actors' School.

04:16.632 --> 04:18.467
No, after-school. After.

04:19.593 --> 04:21.845
-Anyhow, it's for 12 people, right?
-Yes.

04:21.929 --> 04:24.014
It's that table over there.

04:24.098 --> 04:25.224
What are you doing there?

04:30.980 --> 04:32.106
Look at this place.

04:33.065 --> 04:33.899
Enjoy.

04:33.983 --> 04:35.567
-Amazing.
-Oh, what's that?

04:35.651 --> 04:37.361
-Looks great.
-Thank you.

04:37.444 --> 04:38.696
-It looks so good.
-I can't wait.

04:39.571 --> 04:40.864
You all worked really hard.

04:41.740 --> 04:42.574
Shall we toast?

04:42.658 --> 04:43.575
-Yes, sir.
-Sounds good.

04:44.284 --> 04:45.119
Great job.

04:45.202 --> 04:46.870
-Thank you!
-Thank you!

04:48.080 --> 04:50.249
Why are you two so dressed up today?

04:50.332 --> 04:52.084
I know, why are you looking so cute?

04:52.960 --> 04:54.294
It's the weekend.

04:55.671 --> 04:57.256
Awesome.

05:03.929 --> 05:05.139
It's so delicious, sir.

05:05.973 --> 05:08.350
How's the date going? Send me a pic.

05:09.268 --> 05:11.228
Sir, can I have some of this?

05:11.311 --> 05:13.147
-Sure, dig in.
-Yes!

05:13.230 --> 05:14.648
-Is it good?
-I want some too.

05:14.732 --> 05:18.610
Let's get a group pic for the memories.

05:18.694 --> 05:20.738
-Great!
-Good idea.

05:20.821 --> 05:21.905
-Let's do it.
-Yeah.

05:21.989 --> 05:23.240
We have to for sure.

05:26.535 --> 05:27.536
Hey, I'm barely in the photo.

05:27.619 --> 05:30.581
One, two, three.

05:30.664 --> 05:33.792
WITH MR. GA
AFTER-SCHOOL MATH FINISHED

06:26.970 --> 06:27.930
Dong-ju.

06:30.349 --> 06:31.350
Hey, Dong-ju.

06:33.435 --> 06:34.269
What's up?

06:37.231 --> 06:38.148
I can't see.

06:38.857 --> 06:39.733
What?

06:41.902 --> 06:42.736
Take me to the hospital.

06:43.821 --> 06:45.280
Okay, just a moment.

06:46.532 --> 06:48.700
Hey, Gi-jeon. Wake up.

06:48.784 --> 06:50.035
What is it?

06:50.119 --> 06:50.953
Woo-su isn't well.

07:06.635 --> 07:07.719
I can't see anything.

07:15.310 --> 07:18.397
I see you had a full-thickness
corneal transplant in your right eye.

07:20.107 --> 07:20.941
Yes.

07:21.024 --> 07:25.696
The only thing we can try is
a deep anterior lamellar keratoplasty.

07:25.779 --> 07:28.407
This surgery keeps the endothelium intact

07:28.490 --> 07:30.367
while replacing the rest
in a partial transplant.

07:34.496 --> 07:35.622
Hasn't it been ten years?

07:36.748 --> 07:38.584
He's been fine with no after effects.

07:38.667 --> 07:39.710
I know.

07:41.295 --> 07:42.629
I thought everything was fine too.

07:43.255 --> 07:44.381
Why now?

07:48.343 --> 07:49.178
Hey.

07:49.970 --> 07:50.804
Are you

07:52.306 --> 07:53.265
crying?

07:54.850 --> 07:56.143
What do we do with that idiot?

07:57.269 --> 08:00.189
I knew this would happen when he started
staying up all night reading papers.

08:01.148 --> 08:02.649
I just knew it, damn it.

08:02.733 --> 08:05.152
Why didn't he listen to me
and insisted on becoming a teacher?

08:05.235 --> 08:07.070
He had to give up
his beloved research too.

08:07.154 --> 08:09.239
This whole time, I've been terrified
that this would happen.

08:10.908 --> 08:12.117
He'll be fine.

08:13.660 --> 08:15.621
What happened to teasing
and scrapping with him?

08:15.704 --> 08:17.122
You know

08:17.206 --> 08:18.957
how much Da-ju cares about Woo-su.

08:20.417 --> 08:21.752
TREATMENT ROOM 1

08:28.175 --> 08:29.968
-Take him up to admissions.
-Okay.

08:32.012 --> 08:32.930
Are you okay?

08:33.639 --> 08:34.473
Yeah.

08:35.224 --> 08:36.308
What did they say?

08:36.934 --> 08:38.435
You dumb idiot!

08:39.102 --> 08:41.897
What kind of a perfectionist know-it-all
can't take care of one eye?

08:41.980 --> 08:45.025
You had the time and energy
to nag at everyone else

08:45.108 --> 08:47.152
but couldn't handle your one job, asshole?

08:48.820 --> 08:50.239
He gets it too, okay?

08:50.822 --> 08:52.074
I've decided to get surgery.

08:53.992 --> 08:56.036
Will that fix things?

08:57.955 --> 08:59.915
To be perfectly frank,

08:59.998 --> 09:03.627
the likelihood of your eyesight
returning to what it was before

09:04.544 --> 09:05.754
is 50-50.

09:07.756 --> 09:11.468
Your cornea is so thin
that the circumstances aren't favorable.

09:13.387 --> 09:16.139
Make sure you don't push yourself
before the surgery.

09:16.223 --> 09:17.391
Just rest whenever possible.

09:18.767 --> 09:20.644
I'm going to be admitted

09:20.727 --> 09:22.604
while they assess
whether they can do the surgery.

09:24.564 --> 09:26.400
So stop making a scene and just go home.

09:26.483 --> 09:27.859
Let's go get you admitted.

09:41.415 --> 09:43.792
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

09:43.875 --> 09:45.627
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

09:45.711 --> 09:46.670
Good morning.

09:47.671 --> 09:49.506
Mr. Ga is having trouble with his eyesight

09:49.589 --> 09:51.508
and won't be able to come to school
for the time being.

09:52.134 --> 09:53.760
I'll be covering for him.

09:54.469 --> 09:56.054
Let's start with roll call.

09:57.431 --> 09:58.974
Sir.

09:59.057 --> 10:00.767
How bad is it?

10:00.851 --> 10:02.269
What happened?

10:04.271 --> 10:07.607
You once said that if he overdoes it,
he could risk his other eye.

10:07.691 --> 10:08.859
What did you mean by that?

10:09.443 --> 10:11.278
If he can't come to school
for the time being,

10:11.361 --> 10:12.821
does that mean he's in the hospital?

10:12.904 --> 10:14.656
How long is he going to be there?

10:16.116 --> 10:18.577
Don't you have class, Eui-ju?

10:19.995 --> 10:21.997
Which hospital is he at?

10:22.080 --> 10:25.292
Just tell me. You can tell me that much.

10:28.837 --> 10:30.589
Although your cornea is thin,

10:30.672 --> 10:33.884
it shouldn't prevent us
proceeding with the surgery.

10:33.967 --> 10:37.888
After the surgery, the corneal refraction
and others will show improvement.

10:47.814 --> 10:48.648
Hey.

10:49.733 --> 10:51.068
Are you freaking out?

10:51.151 --> 10:52.319
Why would I be?

10:53.528 --> 10:54.863
You looked like you were dying,

10:55.489 --> 10:56.531
but you seem fine now.

10:58.367 --> 10:59.785
Since you're getting surgery anyway,

10:59.868 --> 11:02.162
can't they do an eye tuck too
to clear your field of vision?

11:04.539 --> 11:06.792
There's no surgery for personality, right?

11:12.756 --> 11:14.424
You are freaking out, dude.

11:15.801 --> 11:16.718
Good luck.

11:16.802 --> 11:18.512
See you later, glasses monkey.

11:19.679 --> 11:20.889
You're not wearing glasses.

11:20.972 --> 11:21.932
Later, monkey.

11:23.683 --> 11:24.559
You're okay, right?

11:26.937 --> 11:27.979
Good luck.

11:28.814 --> 11:29.981
We'll head in now.

11:31.650 --> 11:32.651
See you.

11:32.734 --> 11:34.528
Hey, no tears, okay?

11:36.822 --> 11:37.781
Gosh, what a dork.

11:52.712 --> 11:54.423
-What the heck?
-Hey!

11:55.132 --> 11:56.842
Hey, Eui-ju. Where are you going?

11:56.925 --> 11:58.218
What the heck? Did you see that?

11:58.802 --> 12:01.304
He asked me not to say anything
until the surgery was over.

12:01.972 --> 12:04.850
He didn't want to tell you
for fear you'd worry.

12:04.933 --> 12:06.518
He's in Hana University Medical Center.

12:13.233 --> 12:17.070
Fortunately, the surgery
went better than expected.

12:17.654 --> 12:19.698
Are you in any discomfort?

12:20.282 --> 12:21.658
No, I feel fine.

12:23.118 --> 12:25.704
When will I be able to read again?

12:26.288 --> 12:29.166
It'll probably feel a bit uncomfortable,

12:29.249 --> 12:31.751
but you should be able to read
in about a week.

12:31.835 --> 12:33.920
To be able to see without any discomfort,

12:34.004 --> 12:36.756
you will probably need
about three or four weeks.

12:36.840 --> 12:38.091
I see. Thank you.

12:38.842 --> 12:40.260
Now all you have to do is recover.

13:03.200 --> 13:05.327
Eui-ju, you left early without permission.
Two demerits.

13:15.420 --> 13:16.421
Mr. Ga.

13:17.130 --> 13:18.548
Are you okay?

13:22.719 --> 13:24.763
I asked if you're okay.

13:27.015 --> 13:28.934
About that nonsense
absolute-value problem.

13:32.020 --> 13:33.480
My answer is…

13:38.735 --> 13:40.362
a promise from ten years ago.

13:51.122 --> 13:52.749
Are you in a lot of pain?

13:56.378 --> 13:57.212
YEO EUI-JU

13:57.295 --> 14:01.591
My mom said if I get this wrong again,

14:01.675 --> 14:05.554
she won't let me watch Pichi Pichi Pichi.

14:09.057 --> 14:10.433
Hold your fingers out.

14:11.851 --> 14:14.646
To get 12, you need 2 more fingers
on top of these 10 fingers.

14:14.729 --> 14:17.232
One, two, three, four, five…

14:18.567 --> 14:20.193
-Seven.
-Correct.

14:20.735 --> 14:22.862
Don't try to subtract
from the ones column.

14:22.946 --> 14:25.574
Think of it as subtracting
from the entire two-digit number.

14:25.657 --> 14:30.870
Then the tens column is helping
the ones column, like friends.

14:30.954 --> 14:31.871
What a nice friend.

14:32.914 --> 14:33.748
Right.

14:33.832 --> 14:35.083
Shall we solve another one?

14:35.166 --> 14:38.128
Hey, I might just be a genius.

14:38.211 --> 14:39.796
Math is so easy.

14:41.298 --> 14:45.343
Next time I see you,
I'll show you my perfect score.

14:45.969 --> 14:47.053
I promise.

14:58.690 --> 15:00.609
But what did you say to me
when we met after ten years?

15:01.276 --> 15:02.360
Yeo Eui-ju?

15:03.695 --> 15:05.322
-Yeo Eui-ju!
-Here!

15:06.698 --> 15:07.657
Four points, sir.

15:08.658 --> 15:09.659
Four points in math?

15:12.078 --> 15:13.538
You just hate math?

15:14.706 --> 15:17.751
Do you know how hard I worked
to see you keep that promise?

15:20.420 --> 15:25.425
Wow, it seems some people
are just destined to meet.

15:26.176 --> 15:27.886
It's fate.

15:27.969 --> 15:29.095
What?

15:30.680 --> 15:31.514
Nothing.

15:32.599 --> 15:33.808
Never mind.

15:33.892 --> 15:35.644
I remember now.

15:35.727 --> 15:38.271
So you were that cute guy
who was good at math.

15:38.897 --> 15:40.106
Wow.

15:40.940 --> 15:41.775
Now you remember?

15:42.776 --> 15:44.027
So? I bet that left you speechless.

15:44.110 --> 15:45.111
Just a minute.

15:45.904 --> 15:47.113
Then,

15:47.197 --> 15:50.617
since I met you when I was eight,

15:51.660 --> 15:54.537
that means you met me way before Deul-i.

15:54.621 --> 15:55.497
What?

15:56.539 --> 15:57.999
Score one for me.

15:59.709 --> 16:00.835
You really are something.

16:03.588 --> 16:04.839
So,

16:04.923 --> 16:06.257
isn't she coming to see you?

16:06.841 --> 16:07.842
Why would she?

16:07.926 --> 16:10.887
Aren't you two dating?

16:11.471 --> 16:12.764
As if. We're just friends.

16:13.431 --> 16:14.641
I don't think so.

16:14.724 --> 16:17.268
You look completely different
when you're with her.

16:17.352 --> 16:20.188
You smile a lot, and sweetly too.

16:20.855 --> 16:22.941
So you don't smile
when you're with your friends?

16:23.900 --> 16:25.193
I guess that makes sense.

16:26.903 --> 16:28.655
Then, can I

16:28.738 --> 16:30.448
still have some hope?

16:31.032 --> 16:31.908
For what?

16:33.702 --> 16:34.536
Never mind.

16:35.662 --> 16:37.122
Get well soon, sir.

16:39.207 --> 16:40.542
Get out of here. I'm tired.

16:42.085 --> 16:43.169
Yes, sir.

16:45.046 --> 16:45.922
Goodbye.

16:46.005 --> 16:47.674
Eui-ju, can you put this down
before you go?

16:48.508 --> 16:49.759
Sure!

16:50.635 --> 16:51.761
I'm home.

16:52.846 --> 16:53.680
-Hey, Mom.
-Yeah?

16:53.763 --> 16:55.014
-Mom.
-What?

16:55.098 --> 16:56.516
Back in the day,

16:56.599 --> 17:00.311
when I went to the hospital in Seoul,
what hospital was I in?

17:00.895 --> 17:04.691
What in the world are you talking about?

17:04.774 --> 17:08.445
You know, when I went to the hospital
in Seoul back in first grade.

17:08.528 --> 17:10.655
Why would you go to the hospital?

17:10.739 --> 17:12.490
I am a pharmacist, you know.

17:12.574 --> 17:15.326
You've never been sick enough
to go to the hospital.

17:16.578 --> 17:18.371
Yes, I have.

17:21.708 --> 17:22.542
Never?

17:23.251 --> 17:24.169
Never.

17:27.172 --> 17:29.382
Dad, have I never been to the hospital?

17:32.093 --> 17:32.927
Huh?

17:33.720 --> 17:34.637
What the heck?

17:35.680 --> 17:36.639
What was that then?

17:38.933 --> 17:40.393
Was it someone else?

17:43.563 --> 17:45.523
Mr. Ga, at a young age,

17:45.607 --> 17:48.109
you became famous
for being a math prodigy.

17:48.193 --> 17:49.736
CHAPTER 51:
THE NONSENSE ABSOLUT VALUE

17:49.819 --> 17:52.447
Is there a reason
you decided to become a teacher?

17:55.492 --> 17:57.952
Right before the second Math Olympiad,

17:58.036 --> 17:59.370
I decided to withdraw.

18:00.455 --> 18:02.499
Officially, it was because
of my worsening eyesight,

18:03.416 --> 18:05.543
but in truth, there was another reason.

18:05.627 --> 18:07.712
While I was over at the training camp,
I met this friend.

18:07.796 --> 18:09.172
GA WOO-SU
MATH TEACHER, MURIM GIRLS' HIGH

18:09.255 --> 18:11.216
That person overslept
and was late every day.

18:11.299 --> 18:13.927
They were even caught reading comics
when we were solving problems.

18:14.552 --> 18:18.473
Watching them solve problems quickly,
even the ones I couldn't work out…

18:18.556 --> 18:19.390
Bang.

18:19.474 --> 18:20.683
…baffled me for the first time.

18:22.727 --> 18:26.231
That person had incredible intuition
and obviously enjoyed math.

18:26.314 --> 18:29.150
I realized I would meet
many similar people,

18:30.318 --> 18:32.445
and I suffered a crisis of confidence.

18:32.529 --> 18:34.197
I was at a loss about my next step.

18:35.156 --> 18:36.825
After telling people I was dropping out,

18:36.908 --> 18:38.868
I went to the hospital
to have surgery on my eye.

18:39.452 --> 18:42.413
And I ran into a little girl.

18:44.499 --> 18:46.251
When I saw how her eyes shone,

18:46.835 --> 18:48.670
and how she jumped around in excitement,

18:49.796 --> 18:53.299
I was reminded of the moment
when math first sparked my interest.

18:54.342 --> 18:55.844
I had only ever learned before,

18:56.469 --> 18:58.429
and that was the first time I found joy

18:59.180 --> 19:01.140
in teaching someone else.

19:03.017 --> 19:04.185
Then, that little girl

19:04.269 --> 19:06.479
must have gone on
to compete in the Olympiad like you

19:06.563 --> 19:09.190
and become really great at math.

19:11.693 --> 19:12.569
Well.

19:13.695 --> 19:15.738
Life doesn't always turn out
how you expect.

19:20.493 --> 19:21.619
She's lost it.

19:22.996 --> 19:24.038
One final question.

19:24.873 --> 19:28.334
What does math mean to you, Mr. Ga?

19:31.588 --> 19:33.965
TEACHERS' OFFICE

19:35.466 --> 19:36.467
Math…

19:39.178 --> 19:40.680
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

19:41.723 --> 19:42.599
Good morning.

19:43.224 --> 19:44.183
Math

19:45.810 --> 19:46.811
is the process

19:47.437 --> 19:49.564
of constantly discovering my own limits.

19:58.531 --> 19:59.365
Good morning.

19:59.449 --> 20:01.618
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

20:08.499 --> 20:10.168
I got 55 points.

20:19.844 --> 20:22.388
Great job on making it through
another year of boring school.

20:22.472 --> 20:24.807
Yes, sir, we did do an amazing job.

20:24.891 --> 20:26.351
-Great job, everyone!
-Great job!

20:26.434 --> 20:28.561
-Guys, well done!
-Great job!

20:28.645 --> 20:31.105
-Good work.
-Great job!

20:31.189 --> 20:32.941
Now you're all seniors.

20:34.734 --> 20:37.153
If you spend the vacation chilling,
you'll regret it come March.

20:37.862 --> 20:39.906
I'm not saying
you should do nothing but study.

20:39.989 --> 20:42.784
Take some time to figure out
what you like and dislike,

20:43.409 --> 20:45.536
what you're good at,
and what you want to do.

20:46.120 --> 20:48.539
Check on yourself at all times
and get to know yourself better…

20:55.630 --> 20:56.589
and move forward.

21:01.552 --> 21:04.389
I hope you will walk the path
of your choice with confidence,

21:04.472 --> 21:06.474
regardless of what others say.

21:11.229 --> 21:12.355
You are

21:13.439 --> 21:14.273
all…

21:16.693 --> 21:18.236
stars with your own light.

21:20.989 --> 21:22.281
-Oh, Mr. Ga.
-How sweet!

21:38.339 --> 21:39.382
Class dismissed.

21:40.425 --> 21:43.011
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

21:51.019 --> 21:52.020
CHAPTER 52:
I'M GLAD WE MET

21:52.103 --> 21:54.397
-What do you think?
-It's great.

21:54.480 --> 21:57.692
"You and I, our hearts so close."

21:58.484 --> 21:59.736
"Like orbiting stars,

22:00.486 --> 22:02.155
distant for a spell but close for ages."

22:03.865 --> 22:04.824
-What do you think?
-Wow.

22:04.907 --> 22:06.534
Eui-ju, Go-ya.

22:07.201 --> 22:09.120
-You two have talent.
-You guys killed it.

22:09.203 --> 22:10.872
-Props. Respect!
-It's amazing.

22:11.497 --> 22:12.623
-It's so cool.
-I love it.

22:12.707 --> 22:14.333
-The best.
-We did slay this.

22:14.876 --> 22:16.502
"Orbiting stars," that's totally us.

22:16.586 --> 22:19.255
-Yeah, for real.
-Oh, Eui-ju.

22:20.590 --> 22:23.092
I'll definitely come visit, okay?

22:23.176 --> 22:24.093
Make it soon.

22:24.177 --> 22:25.636
Got it. I'll be on the next plane.

22:27.305 --> 22:28.389
Jenny.

22:29.223 --> 22:30.641
Don't forget us.

22:32.435 --> 22:34.854
And don't leave the group chat, okay?

22:35.438 --> 22:37.940
I'm going to spam you
with emojis all the time.

22:38.024 --> 22:39.192
Please do.

22:41.819 --> 22:42.987
Take care, Jenny.

22:45.073 --> 22:47.909
Get yourself a boyfriend
before you come back.

22:50.203 --> 22:51.079
Okay.

22:51.162 --> 22:52.997
What's taking Eui-ju so long anyway?

22:53.498 --> 22:54.332
There she is now.

22:55.541 --> 22:56.834
-Get a move on!
-Hurry up!

22:56.918 --> 22:57.960
You're late!

22:58.044 --> 22:59.378
What took you so long?

22:59.462 --> 23:00.463
Ji-a said…

23:00.546 --> 23:03.549
she wanted to say bye to Jenny,
so I waited for her to get out of work.

23:03.633 --> 23:04.634
Hey, when did I say that?

23:04.717 --> 23:06.010
That's exactly what you said.

23:06.094 --> 23:07.595
Oh, Ji-a.

23:07.678 --> 23:09.013
Ji-a.

23:10.014 --> 23:12.183
I'll never get used to her energy level.

23:12.266 --> 23:13.351
So true.

23:13.434 --> 23:16.020
You guys are like cat and dog.

23:16.104 --> 23:16.979
Meow! Woof!

23:18.231 --> 23:20.566
I'm sorry for not being there for you.

23:21.067 --> 23:22.485
Take care over there.

23:22.568 --> 23:23.778
Here, eat this on the way.

23:26.280 --> 23:27.782
Oh, my seatmate.

23:30.409 --> 23:32.036
-Seatmates.
-Thanks.

23:32.120 --> 23:33.412
Jenny, I got you something too.

23:34.372 --> 23:36.499
Take care and don't forget us.

23:37.083 --> 23:37.917
Okay.

23:39.377 --> 23:40.294
Ta-da!

23:40.378 --> 23:43.381
A STAR FAR AWAY

23:45.174 --> 23:46.843
Awesome!

23:47.969 --> 23:49.095
Eui-ju.

23:52.181 --> 23:54.308
I'm gonna miss you.

23:54.851 --> 23:56.102
For sure.

24:05.945 --> 24:08.406
Hey, I'm over here!

24:09.574 --> 24:11.325
I'm over here.

24:13.244 --> 24:14.579
I love you!

24:15.204 --> 24:17.039
-She's going.
-Bye.

24:17.123 --> 24:18.875
-Bye, Jenny!
-Bye!

24:31.387 --> 24:33.639
I'm glad we met.

24:57.246 --> 24:59.290
Thank you for welcoming me so warmly

24:59.373 --> 25:02.251
and giving me all these special memories.

25:04.295 --> 25:05.213
I'll take a photo of you.

25:05.296 --> 25:06.631
-Good.
-Great.

25:06.714 --> 25:07.965
-Stand here.
-Korea's beautiful.

25:10.843 --> 25:12.428
-I like tteokbokki.
-You like it?

25:12.511 --> 25:15.056
-Tteokbokki is the main event.
-No, it's boring by itself.

25:15.139 --> 25:16.933
-No, that's the best part.
-I like sundae too.

25:17.016 --> 25:19.977
Or what about chicken and pizza?

25:20.061 --> 25:20.937
Oh, right.

25:21.020 --> 25:21.854
As for my novel,

25:21.938 --> 25:25.066
thanks to the supportive readers
fervently hoping for its re-launch,

25:25.149 --> 25:26.442
I finished writing it

25:27.235 --> 25:29.153
and launched it officially.

25:29.237 --> 25:31.530
It hit a million downloads.

25:32.365 --> 25:36.077
I've finally become a mega-hit author.

25:37.119 --> 25:39.580
Oh, you want to know how it ended?

25:40.122 --> 25:43.292
WE WERE FRIENDS, FINAL EPISODE

25:54.595 --> 25:55.554
Fine, I get it.

25:56.430 --> 25:58.808
Now that I've finally realized
that you like Tae-ha,

25:59.725 --> 26:00.977
I'm done.

26:01.060 --> 26:02.520
Si-on.

26:03.479 --> 26:05.022
I said I'd have no regrets.

26:06.065 --> 26:07.066
But I do.

26:09.568 --> 26:11.279
I regret all the cruel words
I said to you.

26:11.362 --> 26:13.072
Thanks for everything, Yoon!

26:13.155 --> 26:15.324
Come on, it's not like
we won't see each other again.

26:15.408 --> 26:16.701
We won't.

26:16.784 --> 26:17.743
Today is the last time.

26:19.078 --> 26:20.121
Is that really necessary?

26:20.204 --> 26:22.748
Si-on, you were my everything
back in high school.

26:24.792 --> 26:26.127
I don't want to lose you.

26:31.007 --> 26:32.591
It definitely seems like I won.

26:33.217 --> 26:35.344
So why do I feel like crap?

26:35.803 --> 26:37.096
You think it's a competition?

26:37.179 --> 26:38.264
So what if you win?

26:38.347 --> 26:39.682
Do you get a medal or something?

26:40.975 --> 26:42.101
You little punk.

26:47.023 --> 26:48.190
Don't.

26:53.029 --> 26:54.155
I'm leaving.

26:54.947 --> 26:56.282
Si-on, wait.

26:56.365 --> 26:57.283
What the heck?

26:58.284 --> 26:59.744
There you all are.

27:01.412 --> 27:03.039
I've been looking for you forever.

27:03.122 --> 27:05.541
Let's all have a seat.

27:08.919 --> 27:11.672
What the heck?
What's with the strained atmosphere?

27:11.756 --> 27:13.549
Did someone die or something?

27:15.801 --> 27:17.470
I'm not in the mood for jokes.

27:18.512 --> 27:19.347
So you got dumped.

27:20.514 --> 27:21.682
You know…

27:22.933 --> 27:24.685
So you're just going to give up?

27:26.395 --> 27:27.271
I…

27:28.272 --> 27:29.774
refuse to give up on Yoon!

27:30.399 --> 27:31.484
Hey, Jae-min.

27:31.567 --> 27:33.444
What? What have you got to say?

27:33.527 --> 27:34.653
Damn it.

27:34.737 --> 27:36.113
Hey, Yoon.

27:36.197 --> 27:38.449
Are you really never going to
see Si-on again?

27:39.200 --> 27:40.034
Of course you are.

27:40.117 --> 27:42.078
You too, Tae-ha.

27:42.161 --> 27:43.954
Can you be happy

27:44.038 --> 27:45.247
when Yoon is so sad?

27:55.716 --> 27:56.926
Let's all move in together!

27:58.886 --> 27:59.929
Huh?

28:00.513 --> 28:02.098
-All of us?
-It's no big deal.

28:03.349 --> 28:04.392
Let's all live together.

28:05.476 --> 28:08.020
You only truly get to know someone
after living together.

28:08.813 --> 28:09.647
That's how

28:11.107 --> 28:12.441
you get to see their true nature.

28:14.110 --> 28:16.654
Still, there's no need
for all of us to live together.

28:17.488 --> 28:18.739
Are you scared?

28:18.823 --> 28:19.657
Then butt out.

28:19.740 --> 28:20.991
Never!

28:22.618 --> 28:23.494
I'm confident too.

28:25.871 --> 28:26.956
This doesn't seem right--

28:27.039 --> 28:28.707
Hush!

28:29.667 --> 28:30.584
Hush!

28:31.168 --> 28:32.002
Don't worry,

28:32.086 --> 28:34.588
my little baby deer.

28:34.672 --> 28:36.006
What?

28:36.632 --> 28:37.633
This is going to be so much fun.

28:39.635 --> 28:40.594
Fun?

28:41.345 --> 28:42.430
It's going to be hell.

28:46.434 --> 28:47.560
Is this the start of round two?

28:51.355 --> 28:52.565
Okay, let's go!

28:53.190 --> 28:55.526
To our home, sweet home!

28:55.609 --> 28:57.403
Yeah! Bang, bang!

28:57.486 --> 28:59.071
Let's go!

29:09.832 --> 29:14.462
MOST POPULAR WEB NOVEL OF 2026
WE WERE FRIENDS

29:14.545 --> 29:17.673
FINAL CHAPTER:
FIRST SNOW

29:18.257 --> 29:19.341
Honey,

29:19.425 --> 29:21.218
when was this taken?

29:22.094 --> 29:23.762
Oh, wow.

29:23.846 --> 29:26.724
That's when I went to the ER
with food poisoning.

29:27.391 --> 29:28.309
The ER?

29:30.227 --> 29:34.732
When you kept feeding me raw oysters,
saying they were good for my stamina.

29:34.815 --> 29:35.816
Man.

29:35.900 --> 29:38.027
Oh, that time when we were up in Seoul?

29:53.250 --> 29:54.293
What brings you here?

29:56.170 --> 29:57.630
You're leaving tomorrow, right?

29:57.713 --> 29:59.006
Have you finished packing?

29:59.632 --> 30:01.759
Yeah. Are you here to say goodbye?

30:04.595 --> 30:06.222
I'm here to give you this.

30:14.146 --> 30:17.274
I heard hospital bills in America
are really expensive,

30:17.358 --> 30:20.194
and it can be hard to get hold
of medicine. What if you get sick?

30:23.030 --> 30:24.657
Don't get sick.

30:24.740 --> 30:28.536
And don't get too close to Deul-i
while you're there.

30:28.619 --> 30:32.414
Then again, don't get too close
to any American girls either.

30:32.915 --> 30:35.459
Just focus on your studies, okay?

30:36.126 --> 30:37.378
Also,

30:37.461 --> 30:39.880
watch out for pretty American girls…

30:40.464 --> 30:44.260
and handsome American guys as well.

30:44.343 --> 30:48.305
If anyone talks to you,
don't smile back at them.

30:48.389 --> 30:49.431
Okay?

30:52.059 --> 30:53.018
Thanks.

30:55.604 --> 30:57.815
That's exactly the smile
I'm talking about.

30:58.440 --> 31:00.442
This is going to be a disaster.

31:02.736 --> 31:05.447
You're only staying in the US
during the vacation

31:05.531 --> 31:07.283
to conduct research, right?

31:07.366 --> 31:08.659
You have to come back.

31:10.119 --> 31:11.453
Talk about overthinking.

31:12.371 --> 31:13.831
Good luck with your writing.

31:14.623 --> 31:15.624
What's your next novel about?

31:19.086 --> 31:20.296
The title is…

31:38.314 --> 31:39.607
Have a great trip.

31:40.983 --> 31:43.402
Thanks. Look after yourself.

32:44.421 --> 32:46.632
Mr. Ga!

32:47.216 --> 32:48.467
Come here, sir!

32:49.635 --> 32:51.261
Look, it's snowing!

32:51.345 --> 32:52.388
Snow! It's the first snow!

32:53.055 --> 32:53.972
First snow.

32:57.017 --> 32:58.435
It's snowing!

32:59.269 --> 33:01.230
It's the first snow!

33:07.027 --> 33:08.028
Do you like it that much?

33:11.407 --> 33:12.616
Of course!

33:13.409 --> 33:15.285
It's my first snow!

33:15.953 --> 33:16.995
First snow!

33:18.080 --> 33:19.039
My first snow!

34:03.167 --> 34:05.252
-Rock, paper, scissors!
-Rock, paper, scissors!

34:05.335 --> 34:07.755
-Rock, paper, scissors!
-Rock, paper, scissors!

35:10.901 --> 35:12.986
Everything is sweet and sour

35:14.655 --> 35:17.032
This might be the real me

35:18.617 --> 35:21.328
Everything is sweet and sour

35:21.787 --> 35:23.789
Fill it sweetly

35:23.872 --> 35:25.624
Sweet and sour

35:52.901 --> 35:56.947
-So cute!
-So cute!

35:57.030 --> 35:59.157
-Jenny!
-Jenny!

36:09.084 --> 36:10.961
What's really on your mind

36:11.044 --> 36:12.629
If you feel uneasy

36:12.713 --> 36:14.464
You know it's all right

36:14.548 --> 36:17.050
When you look up to the sky

36:17.134 --> 36:20.220
It's sweet and sour

36:20.304 --> 36:22.556
Everything is sweet and sour

36:23.599 --> 36:26.310
This might be the real me

36:27.769 --> 36:30.022
Everything is sweet and sour

36:30.772 --> 36:32.649
Fill it sweetly

36:32.733 --> 36:34.568
Sweet and sour

36:46.914 --> 36:47.915
-Bye!
-Bye!

36:49.791 --> 36:51.668
-Bye!
-Bye!

36:54.379 --> 36:57.132
THE END

36:57.215 --> 36:59.217
Subtitle: Paul Carver
